n be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (3+18+11+8+7+18+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 77 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot ({3}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{11}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{12}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (9+324+121+64+49+324+144) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 1035 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035-847}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{188}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262358 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1089 "q-263257" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1100 "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n9,\\,13,\\,2,\\,14,\\,7\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1113 #uuid "14f344a6-c26a-52b2-b90a-ff911d074c1c" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262357 1145 "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (9+13+2+14+7) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 45 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({9}^{2}+{13}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{7}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (81+169+4+196+49) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 499 \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}-{(9)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}-81 \\\\  & =\\frac{499-405}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{94}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262359 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262360 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1041 "field-1" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262360 13194139533867 true] [17592186262358 1110 #uuid "1d5e2ddd-96c4-5c5d-847f-d583fda88aa3" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262359 1034 "23.5" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533867 true] [17592186262359 1111 #uuid "bdb66389-ff3e-5b1c-a505-e2be3bdfeafc" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262360 1034 "18.8" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533867 true] [17592186262360 1111 #uuid "5635cbe5-baa1-52c2-a4cc-627869cb0591" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262361 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262362 13194139533867 true] [17592186262361 1089 "q-263302" 13194139533867 true] [17592186262361 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533867 true] [17592186262361 1100 "Compute the vari